  "notes": [
   "Steps 1-3 recorded (chassis brick, two wheel-holder plates underneath, and the hinged yellow cab base). Steps 4-8 on this page are too small to identify reliably, so they are not recorded.",
   "Step 3 yellow assembly is a best guess: gray 92582 hinge plate hinged to a yellow 44302a hinge plate, with a yellow 3022 plate. Exact placement is uncertain.",
   "The wheel-holder plates sit beneath the brick, so they are recorded as other_joins (stud to anti-stud) rather than rests_on.",
   "Page 2 has steps 9-12 and a back-cover ad (no pieces). Step 9 only rotates the boom down, so it adds nothing.",
   "b7 (yellow hinge brick, the boom) was built in steps 4-8 on page 1, which I did not record. I added it here so the boom hinge joins have an endpoint. Its hinge ports and which end faces b4 are assumed.",
   "Step 10 shows two yellow hinge plates. I recorded both as 44302a, which overruns the parts list (2 in total, and b5 on page 1 is a guessed 44302a). Their hinge ordering is a best guess.",
   "Step 11 sub-steps are hard to read. I read sub-step 1 as a 1x2 plate (b10) under the black hinge plate (b11), sub-step 2 as the cone (b13) on the 4595 brick (b12), and sub-step 3 as a grille tile (b14) on b12. The links from b11 to b12 and from b10 to b11 are not given as edges, only b12/b14 rests_on. The cone-to-side-stud join is approximate.",
   "The 4 wheels sit on the wheel-holder plates b2 (b15, b16) and b3 (b17, b18). Each tyre is joined to its wheel.",
   "The minifigure in step 12 is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded.",
   "This is the full corrected graph for both pages. I re-sent everything so the ids and types stay consistent with the parts list (36 pieces).",
   "The 44302a overcount came from my own guesses. b5 is now the yellow 30387 hinge brick, which is the boom (hinged to b4). The earlier extra b7 (30387) is gone. The id b7 is reused for the first 60897 clip plate, and the old b4-b5 and b7 hinge edges were replaced. The only 44302a pieces are b8 and b9 (boom plates).",
   "The 6 separate groups are now joined: the cab, boom, drill, tools and wheels all connect to the chassis b1 through stacking, hinge or clip edges. The booklet builds one model only.",
   "The page images for steps 4-8 are small, so the placement and exact studs for b7, b28, b29, b31, b32, b33, b34, b35, b36, b26, b27, b24, b25 and b30 are best guesses. Only piece types and counts are certain. They follow the parts list and the visible cab, hood, roll bar, levers and clip pieces.",
   "Port names in the stacking edges are approximate (for example stud.1.x on the 1x4 hinge brick). Edges that use a null port are used where the catalogue has no matching port, such as the wheel pin-hole and tyre joins.",
   "The minifigure is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded."
  ]
 },
